{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions","id":1341778,"title":"What's Changed Between Editions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-16T21:25:07-07:00","id":1341778,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What's Changed Between Editions?","content":"It's been a LOOONG time since I've even looked at Exalted, so I'm wondering what's actually changed between 2.5 and 3e. More specifically, what new design space is present in the Solar charm trees? I've seen a couple cross-ability charms, but what else? Also, what, if any, design space has been lost? Can a Dawn of sufficient puissance still blow up a mountain with their sword or bow? Can an Eclipse still make a whole city disappear? (I think this was a charm at one point. Cast Out Beyond Regard maybe?)<br /> <br /> What new toys did we get and what was given away to Goodwill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T21:40:36-07:00","id":1341783,"title":"","content":"From a mechanical standpoint Solars tend to be less able to be built so that you're invulnerable to anything short of Celestial Incarna like you could do in 2.5, but the charm space has opened up quite a bit. God-King's Shrike lets you proclaim a doom upon an entire kingdom and a week later said doom happens. Speaking of doom, Dual Magnus Prana lets you have Doctor Doom style Doombot clones, that if you ever die are retroactively activated.<br /> <br /> Socialize now lets you have an entire roster of characters in your pocket that you can just become whenever you want. So you can have an entire party all to yourself. You can move so fast that you get anime-style duplicates of yourself, they can hide inside somebody's soul with stealth. In general with the way Martial Arts, Sorcery and Evocations have opened up that makes a lot of stuff possible. A Solar with a blue jade daiklave can freeze opponents in ice and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> The really big wide effects tend to be gone though. Like you can't just cure a city of 100,000 people of plague in an instant, you can't juggle mountains, you can't rip the moon out of the sky smack it like a baseball into the sun and blow them both up or anything like that. Also social interaction got a lot of changes. Solars can, basically, no longer just snap their fingers and mind control people with Presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> The design goal was, I think, to take out effects that were so large and sweeping that they just skipped interesting stories with the activation of a single charm, and also making sure that actions had consequences. It was mostly a success. There's some combos out there that can make you invincible, or can basically give you mind control powers, but they seem more like unintentional effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T23:17:31-07:00","id":1341801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions#post1341778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what's actually changed between 2.5 and 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, this'll take awhile. Let me get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T23:48:01-07:00","id":1341806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions#post1341778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What new toys did we get and what was given away to Goodwill?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what DrLoveMonkey already said, which is substantially accurate, here's some other stuff that got given out:<ul><li>Most artifacts now come with Evocations, essentially small charm trees that enhance the use of the artifact and make it feel more thematic. This does mean that designing your own artifacts (at least at the 3 dot and higher levels) requires more homebrewing, but there's already a considerable number of examples, from the Core book, the new Arms of the Chosen artifact sourcebook, and in the so-far released Dragonblooded sourcebook and the upcoming Lunars book. Evocations, I feel, are an excellent way to balance artifacts' power, and really give them each a unique feel (something that 2e claimed to want, but never really delivered on, in my opinion).</li> <li>All the Solar Castes now have more Caste abilities to choose from (each gets to pick 5 from a possible list of 8), meaning that it's easier to build more diverse and useful examples of all the Castes (Dawns are no longer restricted to having two or three caste abilities that will be pretty much redundant with their existing ones, for example).</li> <li>All the Abilities have a bunch of Solar charms for each, meaning that if you want to be a dedicated specialist in any given Ability, the core book has you covered. I think <i>every</i> Ability now has the potential to spend all of your starting Charms in it, and still not completely run out.</li> <li>Along the same lines, every Solar now chooses one of their Caste Abilities as Supernal, which allows them to ignore the usual Essence prereqs for charms in that Ability, meaning they can hit the top tier of power in that one area right out of the gate.</li> <li>The new combat engine has some warts, but it's a vast, vast improvement over the old 2e combat system. It's basically eliminated the old issue of all characters being eggshells with rocket launchers, where any hit would splatter you. Ox-Body Technique is actually a <i>useful charm</i> now! And it's actually made many mortal characters into significant threats against Exalts, at least those who aren't totally combat optimized. Gone are the days when a charm to make you more-or-less immune to the finest mortal swordswoman was an Essence 1, Melee 2 or 3 dip purchase. At the same time, while mortals are a threat, they're not absolutely lethal either, meaning a non-combat-optimized character can exist and survive a battle.</li> <li>The map of Creation has been notably expanded, and several areas that were previously rather undetailed have been given major new terrain features. In particular, the Southeast now has a major body of water, the Dreaming Sea, and the Northeast has a major extension of the old White Sea, the Fang Lakes. Also, there's an island continent in the Southwest, the Caul, which is a major battleground between the Realm and the Lunars.</li> </ul><br /> As for what was &quot;given away&quot;, well, there's nothing I personally consider a big loss. But for the sake of presenting a clear picture, here are some things that have gone:<ul><li>The &quot;magitech&quot; aesthetic of a lot of artifacts has been removed or downplayed. Something that is &quot;First Age Artifice&quot; no longer means it requires a bit more maintenance and is something that behaves like 21st Century technology, but with more gold and essence circuitry. Instead, &quot;First Age Artifice&quot; now applies to artifacts that specifically require major infrastructure to create and support, and is generally only applied to artifacts that the designers think will throw off the intended setting feel if they're easily reproduced. Note that, while the designers have dialed back the &quot;magictech&quot; in descriptions, it's perfectly easy to add it back in if you like it. It just doesn't have much mechanical impact.</li> <li>The designers have decided that largely they <i>aren't</i> going to explain a bunch of metaphysical stuff that they don't think needs explaining. &quot;What is an Exaltation&quot;, for example, is probably not something that's going to get a writeup, and the details and history of the primordial war is not going to get a bunch of wordcount devoted to it, nor is the First Age.</li> <li>In the same vein, the writers are deliberately trying to give the sense that there's lots of blank spaces on the map for STs to fill in, and attempting to keep a sense of the scale of Creation. Expect fewer regional descriptions to mention locations thousands of miles away as trading partners (looking at you, 2e writeups for the Lap and Gem), and devote more wordcount to describing local neighbors.</li> <li>The devs have also said they're going back to the Yozi descriptions from 1st Edition largely, particularly their descriptions in Games of Divinity. Expect a lot of the 2e characterizations (particularly the Ebon Dragon as &quot;basically petty folklore Satan&quot;) to get discarded.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T01:14:02-07:00","id":1341812,"title":"","content":"Oh speaking of artifacts, magic materials and their bonds with exalts have changed a bit. Essentially Exalt types are either neutral, dissonant, or resonant with a magic material. Generally speaking you go with the dominant MM when judging which quality you're dealing with, so if you have say green jade armor with soulsteel inlays its a jade artifact despite the presence of soulsteel.<br /> Exalts and resonance chart:<br /> Solars: Resonant all<br /> Lunars: Resonant Moonsilver; Neutral everything else.<br /> Sidereals: Resonant Star Metal; Dissonant everything else<br /> Dragonblood: Resonant Jade; Dissonant Soul Steel; Neutral everything else<br /> Abyssals: Resonant Soul Steel; Neutral the rest<br /> Liminals: Neutral Soul Steel; Dissonant all things not listed<br /> Getimians: See Sids<br /> Exigents: varies exalt to exalt<br /> <br /> Oh I'm 95% sure Yellow Jade is no longer a thing that exists.<br /> <br /> We also have some more exalt types however not going into that much since not sure how relevant it is to the specific asking of this question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T01:50:59-07:00","id":1341816,"title":"","content":"You know, I can't do it right now, but it seems to me that the most efficient way to break down the changes and additions would be book by book, chapter by chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:04:07-07:00","id":1341818,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure I read a thread somewhere of someone reading exalted 3e chapter by chapter and comparing to 1e and 2e but I don't remember where I read it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:22:19-07:00","id":1341820,"title":"","content":"&quot;Can a Dawn of sufficient puissance still blow up a mountain with their sword or bow?&quot;<br /> No. How were you doing this before?<br /> <br /> A Dawn archer, right off the bat at character creation, can fire her iconic anima out of a bow, slaying an entire army and burning away their souls in the blazing light of the sun.<br /> <br /> A Dawn swordfighter can cut through stone walls and steel gates, duel armies and face down gods and demons. But no mountain destroying effects.<br /> <br /> &quot;Can an Eclipse still make a whole city disappear?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also no. (And again, I don't remember that Charm in 2E.) They can make an entire kingdom run smoothly and become immune to the Wyld, Shadowlands and disease with a single Charm use though.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Combat is very different. Initative now acts like ablative armor (a bit like the HP/Wounds dichotomy in the older Fantasy Flight Games/Dungeons the Dragonning), and fluxuates up and down representing the swing of combat. Ox-body Technique and <i>Soak</i> are now really important. (Hardness is still pretty worthless.) Perfect Defences exist but are no longer your go-to: they can only be used a limited number of times. Stunts don't recover motes, but everyone gets 5m every round. Stunts are more powerful. Multiple actions are basically gone outside of rare powerful Charms (Solars get loads of multiple attack options, because Solars). Combat is just generally more interesting and dynamic now.<br /> <br /> Social interaction has changed so you can only be persuaded to do something if it fits with what your character cares about. Solars get a lot of dickery in this, including making people care about them simply by working out what else they care about, exploiting what a character <i>used</i> to care about, changing what the Solar cares about on the fly and bypassing sexual orientation. But Solars still have to work the system, same as everyone else -- no instant mind control because you rolled 30 successes. The social system is much improved.<br /> <br /> Craft is... just terrible now. If you want to build a diaklave, first you have to build a dozen horseshoes -- then actually use those horse shoes in play to advance the story. Then you can build a dozen normal swords, which also have to actually be used in play. Then you can attempt to make a diaklave... if you have purchased at least 4 dots in Craft: Swords (not &quot;Craft: Fire&quot;, or &quot;Craft: Blacksmithing&quot;, but Craft: Swords), and at least 3 dots in Lore and Occult, then you can start to buy dots in Craft: Artifact (and use the lower of Craft Artifact and Craft Swords on your roll). Crafting a diaklave takes three months, during which time you can't Craft anything else, and need to spend several hours a day working on it (not sped up by Craftsman Needs No Tools). And you do this every time you want to make something. Or repair something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-17-2019, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:40:21-07:00","id":1341822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341820#post1341820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dawn archer, right off the bat at character creation, can fire her iconic anima out of a bow, slaying an entire army and burning away their souls in the blazing light of the sun.<br /> <br /> A Dawn swordfighter can cut through stone walls and steel gates, duel armies and face down gods and demons. But no mountain destroying effects.<br /> <br /> Also no. (And again, I don't remember that Charm in 2E.) They can make an entire kingdom run smoothly and become immune to the Wyld, Shadowlands and disease with a single Charm use though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. How did you get this? Especially the immune to disease thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:44:30-07:00","id":1341823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341820#post1341820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Can an Eclipse still make a whole city disappear?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also no. (And again, I don't remember that Charm in 2E.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in DotFA.<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to say that none of the DotFA stuff has really been brought across.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you have purchased at least 4 dots in Craft: Swords (not &quot;Craft: Fire&quot;, or &quot;Craft: Blacksmithing&quot;, but Craft: Swords), </div> </div> </div>Craft: Weaponsmithing actually. I personally think that's too restrictive and it should be Blacksmithing, but anyway, that's what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crafting a diaklave takes three months, during which time you can't Craft anything else, and need to spend several hours a day working on it (not sped up by Craftsman Needs No Tools). </div> </div> </div>This is technically true, but I think misleading for the reader, as it's now the charm after Craftsman Needs No Tools that reduces the time taken to make a daiklaive to a few weeks. I made two short daiklaives in a week. And again, there's a charm to let you craft other things at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What new toys did we get</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations have already been mentioned. I had a warstrider that could turn invisible, for example, and my friend's Dawn has soulsteel armour that forces those trying to attack him to bow down before him.<br /> <br /> But another big one is the way sorcery works. Spells are pretty much the same (except you roll to generate special sorcerous motes, rather than use your own, so essentially it can take longer to cast but is effectively free; the wp costs are lower as well, in a slightly complex way). But countermagic is a little different, and a sorcerer can disrupt spells already in play, turning them against their user.<br /> More importantly, all sorcerers get rituals to generate extra sorcerous motes, that represent the way they've learnt sorcery; perhaps they make sacrifices to demons, or burn prayers to a Efreet, or have a channeling artefact, or absorb power from the elements, or have prophetic dreams.<br /> <br /> Also, there's now a relatively freeform sorcerous rituals system, that lets you spend a bit of XP and a lot of time and rolls to create permanent sorcerous effects. Mutant monsters, magical rivers, cursed forests, flying mountains, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:46:38-07:00","id":1341824,"title":"","content":"See look, it's all over the place, haphazard and out of order. Does that not strike anybody as bewildering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:56:54-07:00","id":1341826,"title":"","content":"Things I haven't seen mentioned yet (I'm sure the more exhaustive incoming posts will touch on these):<br /> <br /> Martial Arts don't come in multiple tiers, and like Artifact resonance use Keywords on individual Charms to weaken or strengthen them for different types of Exalted.<br /> <br /> Sorcery was revamped in a bunch of ways. Initiations (how you learned Sorcery) have significant mechanical impact, shaping actions run smoother, and there's a brand new Sorcerous Workings system that adds a freeform element as sorcerers attempt to alter the world around them using occult principles. Thaumaturgy got downplayed a lot (though Exalted that learn Sorcery automatically get Thaumaturgy too).<br /> <br /> Weapons and Armor were simplified significantly two three basic types (light, medium, heavy), and uses Tags to create differences between them instead of different stats.<br /> <br /> In general, there's a lot more attention paid to making sure each Ability has a place to shine mechanically. Bureaucracy stands out as the only real loser here (mostly because the one system where it would make the most sense as the primary Ability to rely on is one of the only times Exalted goes, &quot;nah, screw rolling,&quot;). However this is a mixed bag since this can frequently turn into, &quot;we're sailing now, Sail characters do stuff, everyone else twiddle their thumbs.&quot;<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> The new Crafting system is fairly controversial. Even as someone that's fine with the RAW, they're serviceable instead of good (though I don't think it's a big effort to fix that either).<br /> <br /> The Solar Craft Charms are a hot mess though, and that's grown to be as close to a consensus opinion as you tend to get on the Craft system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T03:03:58-07:00","id":1341827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341824#post1341824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See look, it's all over the place, haphazard and out of order. Does that not strike anybody as bewildering?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think DrLoveMonkey and Kelly covered the basics, which is what you should read first, rather than a really, really long description of everything that's changed, which could be overwhelming.<br /> <br /> Depends on The Free Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T03:23:48-07:00","id":1341829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341827#post1341827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a really, really long description of everything that's changed, which could be overwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or about six paragraphs, just placed in the proper order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T03:49:27-07:00","id":1341831,"title":"","content":"Mountain-shattering isn't really a thing in native charmsets now, but you could probably manage it with a sufficiently powerful daiklave. <br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, also those evocations artifacts get now are mostly what determines their dot rating. one dot artifacts no longer exist, two dot artifacts are simple utility items that don't get evocations. 3 dots and up (which all weapons now are) get progressively more powerful and wide-reaching evocation effects (and also can have more evocations total)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T04:09:04-07:00","id":1341833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341822#post1341822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah. How did you get this? Especially the immune to disease thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Order-Conferring Action - the Solar capstone of the best ability (why oh why is it Water aspected for Deebs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T04:49:11-07:00","id":1341837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341829#post1341829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or about six paragraphs, just placed in the proper order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Kelly did?<br /> <br /> After that it's got a bit messy, admittedly. I'll give it a try.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Chapter 1: Exalts<br /> All your old ones are there, but there are new kinds of Exalts. Exigents (made by lesser gods, so you might be Exalted of a local volcano god and have volcano-themed powers, etc), Liminals (products of botched resurrection attempts; think Frankenstein), and some that we know less about (Getimians, who are kind of anti-Sidereals; Dream-Souled, Hearteaters and Umbrals, which are non-canon optional extras).<br /> <br /> Chapter 2: The Age of Sorrows<br /> The map has been expanded (especially in the corners, for example there's a big sea in the south-east) with lots of new additions.<br /> More pulp and classical influence, less Magitech.<br /> You can see it here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Chapter 3: Character Creation<br /> You get more charms and specialities, and a bit of choice for your Caste abilities (Solars choose 5 of 8; for example Dawns might get Resistance and Dodge. Lunars choose 2 of 3, and 2 favoured). Solars (only) can choose one Caste ability that ignores Essence prerequisites.<br /> <br /> Chapter 4: Traits<br /> Instead of the old 7 dots of backgrounds, you now get 10 dots of Merits, which includes all the old backgrounds plus various permanent merits (fleet-footed, iron stomach, mutations, etc). Languages are now a 1-dot merit rather than from Linguistics.<br /> Most anima powers are roughly similar (combat stuff for Dawns, sneakiness and hiding anima for Nights, toughness for Earths, trickery for Changing Moons, etc). Twilights can now teleport to places of power and make spirits into their familiars.<br /> There's also a bonus XP system (which can't be spent on native charms, just everything else) for stuff like engaging your intimacies in the story or fulfilling your caste's role or helping others with theirs.<br /> <br /> Chapter 5: Systems<br /> Combat has changed a lot; it seems more complex but I find flows better. It's more cinematic, building up the advantage in combat before unleashing your decisive attack. Movement is completely different. You get 5m a turn instead of getting motes from stunting.<br /> The social system is more about intimacies than before, and you can't persuade people to do stuff unless they have a supporting intimacy.<br /> Craft has changed massively, and is very controversial (some love it, some hate it). Basically, crafting artefacts takes less time but requires you to have crafted a whole bunch of regular stuff beforehand to build up Craft points.<br /> Sub-systems (poison, etc) have mostly changed a little.<br /> <br /> Chapter 6: Charms<br /> Basically, there's way more but they're a bit weaker. This applies to Solars, Dragonblood and Lunars. Dragonblood charms are a bit more even in power than before, and the Abilities each have charms of different aspects. Lunar charms are also more even (No Moons are no longer rubbish, essentially).<br /> Lunars can also change the Attribute of some charms with certain spirit shapes (for example, take poison charms as Intelligence and Wits instead of their normal Stamina if your spirit shape is poisonous).<br /> <br /> Chapter 7: Martial Arts and Sorcery<br /> Martial Arts are now the same styles for everybody, but Dragonblood get weaker versions and Solars stronger versions.<br /> Spellshave you roll to generate special sorcerous motes, rather than use your own, so essentially it can take longer to cast but is effectively free.<br /> More importantly, all sorcerers get rituals to generate extra sorcerous motes, that represent the way they've learnt sorcery; perhaps they make sacrifices to demons, or burn prayers to a Efreet, or have a channeling artefact, or absorb power from the elements, or have prophetic dreams.<br /> Also, there's now a relatively freeform sorcerous rituals system, that lets you spend a bit of XP and a lot of time and rolls to create permanent sorcerous effects. Mutant monsters, magical rivers, cursed forests, flying mountains, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Chapter Eight: Antagonists<br /> There's a lot more variation in Antagonists now; more weird and wacky stuff that doesn't fit into god/elemental/demon/etc. Animals have more unique stuff. Spirits don't share a charmset, they have their own. Elementals no longer dematerialise.<br /> <br /> Chapter Nine: Artefacts<br /> The key, as has been mentioned, is all weapons and armour are at least 3 dots, but come with their own sets of charms. So one Warstrider might have charms for unleashing giant essence cannons, while another has a charmset for fighting underwater. One artefact boomerang inflicts madness, while another feeds on blood and helps track murderers.<br /> Also, there's less of a magitek aesthetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> So overall I'd say:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What new toys did we get</div> </div> </div> </div>For Solars, a more flexible choice of abilities, a Supernal ability, charms from your artefact, a lot more (and more functional) Martial Arts styles, sorcerous workings, and a lot more stuff in some of the abilities that only had a few charms before (Investigation, Larceny, Socialise, etc).<br /> <br /> For players generally, a bunch of new Exalt types, but none of them have much in the way of published rules yet (I expect the Exigents kickstarter next Spring).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-17-2019, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T06:42:02-07:00","id":1341847,"title":"","content":"Oh, speaking of anima powers, one big difference is how the Eclipse thing of learning the charms of other things works. <br /> <br /> It's no longer a free for all. Instead they can only learn charms with the Eclipse keyword. Other exalted's native charms will never have this, and are categorically off-limits. For this reason Lunar knacks are gone, and they just have shapeshifting-enhancing charms. Also charms exist that allow non-eclipse solars and lunars to learn eclipse charms too. Dragon blooded getting the same isn't entirely off the table but they didn't provide any in What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T08:00:09-07:00","id":1341860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341820#post1341820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft is... just terrible now. If you want to build a diaklave, first you have to build a dozen horseshoes -- then actually use those horse shoes in play to advance the story. Then you can build a dozen normal swords, which also have to actually be used in play. Then you can attempt to make a diaklave... if you have purchased at least 4 dots in Craft: Swords (not &quot;Craft: Fire&quot;, or &quot;Craft: Blacksmithing&quot;, but Craft: Swords), and at least 3 dots in Lore and Occult, then you can start to buy dots in Craft: Artifact (and use the lower of Craft Artifact and Craft Swords on your roll). Crafting a diaklave takes three months, during which time you can't Craft anything else, and need to spend several hours a day working on it (not sped up by Craftsman Needs No Tools). And you do this every time you want to make something. Or repair something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This description of the craft mechanics ranges from misleading, to outright wrong. I'll aim for a somewhat more objective description.<br /> <br /> Crafting is now organized around a couple of mechanics, &quot;project slots&quot; and &quot;craft experience&quot;. Project slots represent the number of different things you can focus on at once, while craft experience represents artistic inspiration or something similar. Craft projects are broken up into tiers, depending on how complex and important an item is. When you complete a project of a given level, you're awarded a certain amount of craft xp for the same tier and the next higher one, based on the number of basic goals you completed and how well you accomplished it (the basic goals are, more or less, &quot;did you impress someone&quot;, &quot;did you benefit yourself&quot;, and &quot;did you support your own intimacies&quot;). Generally, finishing a couple of projects that meet all three goals will earn enough craft xp to attempt a project of the next highest tier. The project slots mechanic does limit the number of things you can work on simultaneously, but only at the higher tiers, and it's relatively cheap to use craft xp to create new slots, spending your inspiration on doing more work simultaneously, essentially. <br /> <br /> Making artifacts does need a separate Craft (Artifacts) skill. This has prereqs of Lore 3 and Occult 3, just like 2e artifact crafting did. However, those requirements no longer increase for 4- and 5-dot artifacts, meaning anyone capable of manipulating essence can at least attempt them, no special gateway charms necessary. <br /> <br /> Personally, I mostly like the basic craft mechanics (with the exception of having separate Craft Abilities for every type of craft, which I've always disliked in every edition). The craft xp mechanic could be better-named (it leads to some confusion with regular xp, in my experience, and the name doesn't convey the intent very well), but in practice, it basically encourages the craft-focused character to always be looking for reasons in-game to use their craft skills. 2e had a strong incentive to have crafting as a strictly background thing, accomplished only during downtime, and even mundane crafts were usually handled off-screen. The need for craft xp to accomplish higher-tier projects, and the necessity of tying crafts to story-based goals, on the other hand, really ensures that the crafter now actively wants to find reasons to craft stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T08:26:22-07:00","id":1341863,"title":"","content":"I noticed that in Lunars and Dragonblood they talked about &quot;Craft Points&quot; rather than &quot;Craft XP&quot; presumably because Vance and Minton agreed that it was confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T08:35:30-07:00","id":1341865,"title":"","content":"Could anyone tell me what has changed lore wise and setting wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:03:00-07:00","id":1341871,"title":"","content":"Oh, also nothing says you can't craft anything else while you have a daiklave on the go. Just the opposite, you might need to do side projects to get more craft points. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I think at least some of the problems that make JohnDoe244 call craft &quot;Terrible&quot; are self-inflicted. Even the best system won't work well if you apply restrictions that don't actually exist. <br /> <br /> So, lore and setting wise, There's 400 lunars now, starmetal isn't made of dead gods any more, there's new exalted running around, There's a new sea in the southeast, there's a new empire on the coast of that sea called Prasad that's nominally a satrapy of the realm but in practice is basically independent, there's a weird island called the Caul with these shrines on that the lunars and dragonblooded fight over... <br /> <br /> They've kinda torn everything down and are just building up from scratch, really. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:07:36-07:00","id":1341872,"title":"","content":"<u>General Setting :</u><br /> <br /> -Celestials created their Exaltations on their own. While Autochthon might(?) have played a part in them coming up with the concept, he didn't make the Exaltations <u>for</u> them.<br /> <br /> -There are no &quot;small gods&quot; anymore, like a god of a single ordinary tree or a god of a single lamp. Gods are all created by the Celestial Bureaucracy or by powerful magic and Charms.<br /> <br /> -Pure Chaos is no longer a category of Wyld, it stops at the step just before that.<br /> <br /> -The Yozis can never escape Malfeas under any circumstance. This rule is absolute (you can do what you want at your table, but in the canon it's not possible).<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Exalts :</u><br /> <br /> -Exalt Charms plateau at Essence 5, which is more powerful than it used to be. While Exalts get more motes from going higher, E6-E10 Charms are roughly as strong as E5 Charms and more meant to be signature Charms.<br /> <br /> -All Exalts are closer to each other in power. While Solars still sit at the top, non-Solars can occasionally have better rolls/effects than Solars for the things they excel at.<br /> <br /> -Lunars can now gain new Shapes without killing their targets by completing alterate challenges like scaring them to death or beating them at cards.<br /> <br /> -Abyssals should be less beholden to their Deathlords - while being your deathlord's servant is still very valid, there should be more freedom to go out there and do your own thing if you prefer.<br /> <br /> -Infernals are moving away from being strictly the Yozi's minions and more towards the theme of being returning corrupt Solars. Their themes will focus on wielding alien powers. Their caste names are changing (i.e. Fiend is now Penumbra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-17-2019, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:42:41-07:00","id":1341882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341872#post1341872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-There are no &quot;small gods&quot; anymore, like a god of a single tree or a god of a single lamp. Gods are all created by the Celestial Bureaucracy or by powerful magic and Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite that? Because the core book has a god of an individual field; moreover, I've seen nothing to indicate that gods can no longer promote God-Blooded to full divinity or sire god-children through sexual reproduction.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I'd say the thing that got the axe was the idea that <i>every</i> field is <i>definitely always going to</i> have a god actively micromanaging it.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:56:22-07:00","id":1341890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341882#post1341882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cite that? Because the core book has a god of an individual field; moreover, I've seen nothing to indicate that gods can no longer promote God-Blooded to full divinity or sire god-children through sexual reproduction.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I'd say the thing that got the axe was the idea that <i>every</i> field is <i>definitely always going to</i> have a god actively micromanaging it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that gods do not appear spontaneously, I do not know the exact acceptable ways for a god to be born. I'm afraid the exact quote is lost somewhere in ask a dev, this second-hand quote where a poster states they're no longer a thing and Vance doesn't contradict them is the best I've got right now (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1175912#post1175912\">link</a>)<br /> <br /> <i>Edit :</i> Here is a more helpful quote (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1190761#post1190761\">link</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-17-2019, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T10:11:53-07:00","id":1341892,"title":"","content":"It's least gods that have been nixed, I think. You might still have the god of a tree or a house, but no gods of individual rice grains or water droplets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T10:17:00-07:00","id":1341894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341871#post1341871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also nothing says you can't craft anything else while you have a daiklave on the go. Just the opposite, you might need to do side projects to get more craft points. </div> </div> </div> </div>You have three major project slots. You need to use three major slots to make an artifact.<br /> <br /> Sure you can buy more slots with Charms, or with Craft XP. So it's an oversimplification to say you can't Craft anything else. But at this point it's quicker to just buy the book and learn the system.<br /> <br /> I stand by calling the Exalted Craft system the worst Craft system in any RPG of all time. Period. You're entitled to have a different opinion, but frankly &quot;terrible&quot; was my attempt at civility -- this isn't a thread for debating Craft, I'm happy to discuss further in a new thread (but it's an old argument and I don't exactly have any new insights).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341865#post1341865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could anyone tell me what has changed lore wise and setting wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple of minor background characters got gender flipped and Rawar is trans now.<br /> <br /> The timeline of the Realm had a bulldozer driven through it -- all the major events still happened, but at vastly different times now. It's meant to make the Realm more dynamic, bit of an ascending power rather than a stagnant empire. Brilliant idea, but it makes reckoning the canon a little difficult if you're playing a Deeb game. (Solar games on the Threshold don't really care what year Cynis was born in so it makes little odds.)<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think Epitome and Elfive have covered the big changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-17-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T10:53:33-07:00","id":1341899,"title":"","content":"A lot of the changes setting wise are really developers saying that is how they are treating it behind the scenes, or stuff they'll never publish. Number of exalts, least gods, magitech. A lot of this you can freely use the old stuff and be pretty confident that nothing will ever actually get published that directly contradicts it.<br /> <br /> Also, Yozis being able to escape Malfeas was never canon, stop saying that it is a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T11:00:31-07:00","id":1341900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341892#post1341892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's least gods that have been nixed, I think. You might still have the god of a tree or a house, but no gods of individual rice grains or water droplets.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. Small gods yes, &quot;least gods&quot; (which in 2e meant everything from the gods of rice grains and water droplets to the subsentient microscopic gods whose thaumaturgy dictated the laws of physics) no. You can still have hearth gods and field gods and all that fun stuff.<br /> <br /> How gods are created or come into existence is one of those &quot;We're not super interested in detailing it&quot; things, for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T11:13:33-07:00","id":1341902,"title":"","content":"My bad, I was unaware of the distinction between least and small.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341899#post1341899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Yozis being able to escape Malfeas was never canon, stop saying that it is a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase then - there is a conscious effort in 3e to make sure Yozi escape plots like the Reclamation do not swallow the whole setting like they did in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T11:16:22-07:00","id":1341903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341899#post1341899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Yozis being able to escape Malfeas was never canon, stop saying that it is a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yozi escape was always impossible.<br /> <br /> MoEP: Infernals pointed out that the Exalted literally exist to do the impossible, and Yozi escape was carried forwards in Broken Winged Crane and Return of the Scarlet Empress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T12:47:39-07:00","id":1341923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341872#post1341872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Exalt Charms plateau at Essence 5, which is more powerful than it used to be. While Exalts get more motes from going higher, E6-E10 Charms are roughly as strong as E5 Charms and more meant to be signature Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? What does this mean? I know that we don't have any examples to point to, but I don't understand how an E7 or E8 charm would be just as strong as E5. I thought that some of the effects from DotFA would be &quot;put on a higher shelf&quot; so to speak, like from E6 or E7 to E8 or E9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:01:52-07:00","id":1341926,"title":"","content":"I wanted to address the Dawn Caste destroying the mountain because to me it's a good way to highlight some key differences between 2nd edition and Ex3.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition you'd essentially approach the mountain like a big opponent with no ability to evade you but lots of soak and health levels, you'd use your combat charms and try to do enough damage until the ST declares it rubble.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition the most pressing question is &quot;why do you want to attack the mountain?&quot; because inanimate objects aren't normally a part of the combat system, unless that mountain is the slowly awakening form of the demon Chernobog or something like that you don't roll join battle against it. If you're fighting something on the mountain there's a type of special attack intended to make the combat system more cinematic called a Gambit which would allow you to do something like attacking above your opponent to try and cause a rockslide. Finally there's your Feats of Strength/Demolition if there's no fighting involved. A Storyteller might allow this one to happen instantly if there's no meaningful difference between smashing it into rubble in a single blow and demolishing it from the peak down over the course of several weeks.<br /> <br /> Currently I don't <i>think</i> there's a way to do it in 3rd edition but as you can see all three are different prospects. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:15:25-07:00","id":1341929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341923#post1341923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? What does this mean? I know that we don't have any examples to point to but I don't understand how an E7 or E8 charm would be just as strong as E5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;how&quot; is pretty simple. They just don't get stronger. To quote the Lunars draft,<br /> <br /> &quot;This chapter includes ancient Lunars who\u2019ve mastered Essence 6+ Charms. Such Charms don\u2019t represent a new tier of power beyond what Essence 5 Charms are capable of \u2014 rather, they depict these elders\u2019 unique and idiosyncratic capacities, signature feats that define their legend but remain within the bounds of ordinary power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Combined with Supernal, this means that starting Solars have access to the most powerful Charms in the setting, E5 Solar Charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:16:02-07:00","id":1341930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341923#post1341923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? What does this mean? I know that we don't have any examples to point to, but I don't understand how an E7 or E8 charm would be just as strong as E5. I thought that some of the effects from DotFA would be &amp;quot;put on a higher shelf&amp;quot; so to speak, like from E6 or E7 to E8 or E9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 6+ isn\u2019t a new tier of power, but more of a personalized unique set of charms. You keep getting more motes, and you do gain NEW abilities, but not more powerful ones. Also raising Essence above 5 no longer lets you raise attributes and abilities above 5, so any effect that lets off of \u201cAdd dice equal to the lower of Essence or Strength\u201d for example stop gaining power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T14:48:39-07:00","id":1341946,"title":"","content":"&quot;This angelic power might be just a LITTLE out of theme for Solars, but I'm Essence 6, so I can push out the boundaries of Solar themes just a LITTLE bit and go no, this is my angelic power charm.&quot;, essentially.<br /> <br /> It doesn't let you make bigger booms or roll more dice or better dice, it just expands your themes a little in a way congruous with how you've been playing your character the last 80+ sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T14:52:49-07:00","id":1341947,"title":"","content":"I can think of a few methods for Solars and exalts to destroy mountains, but its less using your charms and more demolition with Solar tier sorcery and/or workings. Because I'm going to be honest excavating a passage through a mountain by just focusing death ray on it till its melted through sounds like an awesome explanation of an extended roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T15:02:14-07:00","id":1341951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341903#post1341903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yozi escape was always impossible.<br /> <br /> MoEP: Infernals pointed out that the Exalted literally exist to do the impossible, and Yozi escape was carried forwards in Broken Winged Crane and Return of the Scarlet Empress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good you're familiar with the sidebar that says the Infernal books are written from an Infernal propaganda position and the it is in fact impossible for them to escape. But it is your game so if you want it to work go right ahead.<br /> <br /> Broken Winged Crane was more yozi perspective. Return of the Scarlet Empress services the fan obsession with Yozi escape and took it to far.<br /> <br /> Destroying mountains with your sword isn't outside of Solar design space, but it's not a useful charm to have in the core rulebook. Even in 2e it took years for that charm to show up. There are much better charms to put into melee than &quot; I cut the mountain in two,&quot; and we all know that space was tight in the book anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T16:28:05-07:00","id":1341960,"title":"","content":"We may never see that kind of charm this edition anyway. The ability to sweep your blade across and cut a mountain in half or level a city isn\u2019t totally out of theme with solar powers or anything, but it is one of those powers that really cuts away a lot of epic game potential. Like laying siege to the Imperial City should be one of the greatest feats you could even attempt, not something to be accomplished in a single action with the expenditure of motes and willpower. Breaking the outer wall, yes, shattering every building, no. Even God-Kings Shrike has some fairly hefty and dangerous conditions to it, and even if it goes off there\u2019s no guarantee that powerful cities wouldn\u2019t be able to fend off the doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T16:31:46-07:00","id":1341961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341923#post1341923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? What does this mean? I know that we don't have any examples to point to, but I don't understand how an E7 or E8 charm would be just as strong as E5. I thought that some of the effects from DotFA would be &amp;quot;put on a higher shelf&amp;quot; so to speak, like from E6 or E7 to E8 or E9.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's apparent now that Essence above 5 doesn't really denote ascension into some kind of super-Exalt, but really a signifier for somebody exceptionally accomplished and stylish even among the Exalted. In most respects, their power is more personally focused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341926#post1341926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to address the Dawn Caste destroying the mountain because to me it's a good way to highlight some key differences between 2nd edition and Ex3.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition you'd essentially approach the mountain like a big opponent with no ability to evade you but lots of soak and health levels, you'd use your combat charms and try to do enough damage until the ST declares it rubble.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition the most pressing question is &amp;quot;why do you want to attack the mountain?&amp;quot; because inanimate objects aren't normally a part of the combat system, unless that mountain is the slowly awakening form of the demon Chernobog or something like that you don't roll join battle against it. If you're fighting something on the mountain there's a type of special attack intended to make the combat system more cinematic called a Gambit which would allow you to do something like attacking above your opponent to try and cause a rockslide. Finally there's your Feats of Strength/Demolition if there's no fighting involved. A Storyteller might allow this one to happen instantly if there's no meaningful difference between smashing it into rubble in a single blow and demolishing it from the peak down over the course of several weeks.<br /> <br /> Currently I don't <i>think</i> there's a way to do it in 3rd edition but as you can see all three are different prospects. </div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's also meant to be valid for stunt fodder; that if a fight is taking place at the peak of a mountain, it can be dramatically appropriate for a Solar to cleave the peak of it for some purpose such as riding the rock down the slope, something that makes the scene more exciting and maybe shakes it up a bit while not inherently having a tactical value or attacking the mountain being the point.<br /> <br /> I personally find Essence 6 mountain cutting to be a telling example of examining what it meant for Exalted powers to go so high, because a lot of Abilities only have so much that they can do sensibly. A Charm that does infinite damage to an object because you hit it with a sword ultimately looks like an acknowledgement that there's nowhere to take Melee that is congruent with the rest of the Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:11:40-07:00","id":1341967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341961#post1341961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's also meant to be valid for stunt fodder; that if a fight is taking place at the peak of a mountain, it can be dramatically appropriate for a Solar to cleave the peak of it for some purpose such as riding the rock down the slope, something that makes the scene more exciting and maybe shakes it up a bit while not inherently having a tactical value or attacking the mountain being the point.</div> </div> </div> </div> All three editions of Exalted would expect you to use the mountain as stunt fodder. Third Edition's scenery based Gambits are something of a callback to 1st edition stunting rules which could provide you with the functionality of a weaker charm your character didn't possess rather than just more dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:55:42-07:00","id":1341980,"title":"","content":"Exalts plateau at E5, but they can use Artifacts to push their own limits (this is especially true for DBs whose native Charms are weaker than the Evocations they can unlock from Jade Artifacts).<br /> <br /> For instance an E3 Solar can use the Heaven and Earth Gauntlets to do any of the following :<br /> <br /> -knock back a behemoth into a mountain<br /> -destroy heavy fortifications in a single punch<br /> -divert the course of a river by punching it<br /> -stop an avalanche in its tracks with a well timed punch<br /> -divert the course of the mountain Mostath in a single blow<br /> and other such shenanigans.<br /> <br /> So destroying a mountain in one blow is probably still possible for an Exalt, so long as they find or forge the right artifact for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T00:07:47-07:00","id":1342027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1341865#post1341865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could anyone tell me what has changed lore wise and setting wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>So some summaries here:<br /> <br /> <u><b>General Setting</b></u><br /> There's more world there (<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/exalted-ask-the-devs-pt3-merged-x3.753409/post-19230254\" target=\"_blank\">this post </a>on RPG.net shows that nicely). In fact, a way I generally have been thinking on Creation is that there's more Creation in general. This isn't just in area. There's a lot more <i>in</i> that area according to the books with locations we have had so far.<br /> <br /> There's also more time. The First Age lasted five thousand years this time (about fifteen centuries more than in previous editons) and it has a lot more periods, dyansties, overlapping events, and general &quot;texture&quot; to things. The shape is the same, (pre-history, war, Old Realm, Shogunate, Contagion, Second Age, Time of Tumult) but the details in these is heavily revsied. There's even terms about that show this. We see the term War of the Gods or Divine Revolution instead of Primordial War, for instance. Primordial doesn't even ever show up as a term in the 3e corebook. We just see what they became, and when talked about in the past we just see &quot;enemies of the gods' or &quot;creators of the world&quot;. In any case, a bit with 3e is there's a lot of folks writing it who read a lot of history, see how much you can pack into one area, and kind of write with an idea that you can have a region the size of England and do you know, a whole 20-video series about its first two-thousand years as a thing. (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/DNE4zE40kYM\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>) Or Japan and almost sixty (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/ATnFsFRnRsI\" target=\"_blank\">another link</a>.)<br /> <br /> What is canon more or less has reset. While there are references to 3e takes on things in previous editions, 3e is written more or less with an assumption that previous stuff isn't really for sure canon. And what will be &quot;brought back&quot; is in itself subject to change or draws on particular things, like how Yozis draw on their <b>Games of Divinity</b> presentation primarily, but even things htere could be changed. And some things which got a lot talked on them will probably just be toned down and left for you to use as much or little form before as youw ant, they aren't doing much more with them. (Apparently from some dev statements for example, Paragon's write-up in <b>Dragon-Blooded</b> is probably all we'll se eof it this edition for a while.)<br /> <br /> How the world &quot;works&quot; is a bit different in presentation. A lot of Creation would if you dropped random person in it, looks like Earth. People farm the same way, kilm the same way, build houses the same way. At the same time, they have multiple rituals, daily routines, taboos and such. A big thing with 3e compared to 2e at least, is that in 2e, <i>every single one of these</i> was actually magical for real, did something, and was vital. In 3e, some of them might. Many of them <i>don't</i>. And many people in teh world simply can't tell the difference. Remember that hear on Earth, we have superstitions and such without there really being fairies, ghosts, and spirits. Creation does have these...but it also has things folks <i>thinks</i> are those. I think this implies a lot of the world a bit. It's understandable, but still has its weird. And there are more locations that have their unique weirdness. It's just that not every single solitary thing in the world is unique and weird. Even for people in Creation, Paragon is strange, Halta having talking animals is exotic, and sorcerers are rare and feared. Even though your city has a giant sorcerer tower nailing a behemoth to the ground is an important part of your economy, you probably would find Haslanti airboats <i>completely spectacular</i>. And while you might have some legit gods to deal with, you could still put milk saucers on the window sill. Just in case. (Even if no such beings care in where you live.)<br /> <br /> Creation is also a lot less &quot;on the brink&quot; this time around. Balor was something which has happened once in all of history and before. There will never be another probably. The Yozis will never be free. The Neverborn are impotent and mad, and there is no Oblivion. Creation is less than it was, but what Doom it has is going to be something long in the future, which grinds it away and eventaully has it fade from the light, not some big epic Final Battle. A new Alexanar might rise in one part of Creation to never be heard about in another corner. World's big, world's hard to move around, and a lot can happen in there that's of a massive scale. Kind of with the first point, you have room and you have time this editon .<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dragon-Blooded and the Realm</u></b><br /> Something not talked about is this. In 3e the Realm has a lot bigger emphasis. It is pushed much more as the single axial superpower in the setting, is <i>much</i> stronger politically, militarily, and administratively than in previous editions. A lot of the world's economy and geopolitics have it in there. And so the fact that it's about to rip itself apart in a succession crisis is the big cataclysm in the setting right now. A big thing on de-emphasizing a Seond Balorian Crusade or Deathlords Murder Everything is that you make it so you can focus on more things like htis.<br /> <br /> Timeline of stuff in the Realm is different too. Different houses have pretty different origins, times of formation, and so on. House Iselsi notably tried their coup just over one hundred years ago, not four hundred, and they were not demoted from Great House until about 18 years ago.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are presented as less &quot;disposble&quot; now too. They are still weaker than Solars, but the general power curve is still flat enough that they put up fights and can be threats still. The setting also presents their history very differently. After the War of the Gods, they even went and just found their won kingdoms and states around Creation. The First Age kind of implies Celestial Exalted couried favor with the Dragon-Blooded but they remained largely their own thing. THey probably never had much more numbers than now either and are no less fertile now than before either as a whole. At least, nothing implies this edition they're fallen or lacking in numbers compared to previously.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Exaltation also works a bit different in that it's not infinite. Basically there's a Taoist element called Progenitive Essence wherein once you conceive a child, you need to wait a while to &quot;build up&quot; that Progentive Essence, or the chances of any subsequent children Exalting go down a bit. Usually this takes about ten to twenty years. There's even a term for kids born too early (&quot;leftover children&quot;). Basically if you try to do &quot;breeding camp&quot; stuff like in previous editions your chances of getting any Exalted kids is almost nill. Gotta wait or I guess be super lucky. There's also a stigma that teh children of leftover children are less likely to Exalt (this isn't true, just a bias societally). Basically there's a lot more emphasis on DBs in the Realm being valuable, and DBs throughout history being generally so.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lunar Exalted</u></b><br /> Lunar Exalted also go a lot more focus. Their thesis is &quot;Divien Apex Predator&quot; and they have a lot more focus on being hunters, tricksters, and witches. Their Charms are while not as inddividually storng always as Solars, often comparable, and they do feel much more like peers to Solars, oftne preseting a great deal of <i>flexiblity</i> to Solar raw power and competence.They even just outright equal in some areas. Necromancy is going ot have Circles until further notice according ot the devs, and Lunars equal Solars in that, for instance. Thematic strength matters than Solar supremecy, basiclaly.<br /> <br /> Bond has very different origins. Lunars and Solars were not initially paired, and in fact after the War of the Gods there was war between them on who would rule the world. They formed an alliance, and the marriages and partnerships formed unlocked unplanned synergies between them baically. Not all Lunars had a Bonded Solar either (devs are using 1e numbers, so ~300 Solars, and 300-400 Lunars). The Bond is a bit more symmetrical too. Some Solar Charms work differently against Lunars and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Lunar Castes were changed too. Lunars no longer really have any Wyld taint. Chimerism just means you have a spirit shape that blends features from two or more animals (ie, an actual chimera). They formed their First Age Castes out of synergy with Solars (we don't know what tthey had before that, if any). After the Usurpation, they reforged their Castes to the three we have now on purpose. The Full Moon and No Moon are as much creations fo the Second Age as the Changing Moon. The three we have are just straight-up new Castes.<br /> <br /> Rather than hide in the Wyld, Lunars have basically been running an insurgency against Terrestrial Hegemony since the Usurpation. They moslty worked to destory the Shogunate, but a united Dragon-Blooded Host is you know, a lot of Exalts. Since the Contagion they've been gaining ground glboally, and have held the Realm back, but it's a lot more balanced. Some Lunars think they'll win in not long. Others are cynical that the Realm just wins by not losing. But their main thing is against the Shogunate and its heirs since well, they still try to kill Lunars and Lunars threaten their empires. Basically they are much more tied to Creation's history than before, with a presentation that is meant to put Dragon-Blooded in a place of power, while at the same time, make the Lunar threat to the Terrestrial Hegemony very real. They're the two Exalts that define the political ladnscape of Creation today more than anything.<br /> <br /> In this context the Lunars don't build or support societies for some philoosphical goal of protecting the world. The world will live on. It's pretty much more real politic. Many elder Lunars want the throen of the world that they believe was taken from them. Many younger modern Lunars want to fight the emprie that's defined their lives or affected them in some way.<br /> <br /> Folks covered lotta other good points. Felt these were ones that stood out worth bringing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T03:16:03-07:00","id":1342049,"title":"","content":"Excuse me Blaque but First Age lasted 5 thousands years of 5 hundred years ? A friend told me it was 5 hundred so I was set on this idea for Exalted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T04:36:35-07:00","id":1342053,"title":"","content":"According to Ex3 page 20.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The First Age was an age of wonders and glories long lost to the current age. These splendours flowed from the hands and minds of the Solar Exalted, who ruled the world, its gods, and its Chosen as benevolent masters for <b>five thousand years</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T06:44:04-07:00","id":1342060,"title":"","content":"500 years wouldn't work at all. Way too short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:06:34-07:00","id":1342062,"title":"","content":"Dunno why I had an idea than the world was about 1500 years old or something like that but maybe it's the time of the Usurpation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:18:34-07:00","id":1342064,"title":"","content":"From the end of the Primordial War to the Usurpation was circa-5000 years.<br /> From the Usurpation to the setting's default date was circa-1500 years.<br /> So from the end of the Primordial War to the setting's default date is circa-6500 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> In previous editions, from the end of the Primordial War to the setting's default date was 4999 years, the Usurpation was about 3500 years after the Primordial War, and the Shogunate was anywhere from 450 to 1000 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342027#post1342027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is no Oblivion. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this is true. I think it's just that it's less important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:42:43-07:00","id":1342075,"title":"","content":"They've also decided to leave out any mention of the huge orgy that took place after the genesis of the Dragon-Blooded in 2e; Lilun is going unmentioned, and Desus has been excised from the canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:44:36-07:00","id":1342107,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Lilith's first age husband has been mentioned and is explicitly someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:51:39-07:00","id":1342108,"title":"","content":"If i got the gist of things in the 3e Corebook right, it's also implied that Sorcery might have been discovered and rediscovered by mortals and/or exalts in different eras of Creation's history and from multtiple different sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:13:00-07:00","id":1342113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342064#post1342064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the end of the Primordial War to the Usurpation was circa-5000 years.<br /> From the Usurpation to the setting's default date was circa-1500 years.<br /> So from the end of the Primordial War to the setting's default date is circa-6500 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> In previous editions, from the end of the Primordial War to the setting's default date was 4999 years, the Usurpation was about 3500 years after the Primordial War, and the Shogunate was anywhere from 450 to 1000 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I note this but an edition change is also the name of the war itself. We see War of the Gods or Divine Revolution instead so far. In part It hink to put more emphasis on the gods being the instigators and winners, and also in the general &quot;Let's try to put this word on cold turkey to try and not make it so dominating&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342064#post1342064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure this is true. I think it's just that it's less important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to dig in the Q&amp;A thread, but the implication I got is that it's straight-up not a thing anymore. Or at least, not a huge cosmic force that defines the Underworld, Abysslas, and Deathlords as they did. Basically, there's no big pit they ultimatley toss things into so they can have more focus on non-existential-threat-to-the-world things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:54:42-07:00","id":1342123,"title":"","content":"The change to Oblivion falls into the category of things that aren't going to be written about. The devs and writers will operate under the assumption that Oblivion as the manifestation of nonexistence, but nothing should be written to prevent you from using the old version of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that even considering Oblivion to be a threat to Creation is like having a panic attack about the eventual heat-death of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T14:37:29-07:00","id":1342188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342123#post1342123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The change to Oblivion falls into the category of things that aren't going to be written about. The devs and writers will operate under the assumption that Oblivion as the manifestation of nonexistence, but nothing should be written to prevent you from using the old version of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that even considering Oblivion to be a threat to Creation is like having a panic attack about the eventual heat-death of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what I'm good with. Though it is worth noting that in the second bit there, while it seems liek that would be the case, the way the Deahtlords and Neverborn were presented of wanting ot toss all the world in the perverbial Pit <i>now</i> and as violently as possible, didn't do well on the whole presenting the rest of the world as relevant. There's a difference between fearing about heat death and folks actively trying to go General Jack D. Ripper on everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T17:59:21-07:00","id":1342237,"title":"","content":"Death lords weren't exactly competent in the past. They were all to wrapped up in their passion plays to accomplish anything. The only Deathlord that I recall being more dangerous than an 80's cartoon villain going mwahaha in their secret lair was the Bodhisattva and his First Age Doom Fleet. I doubt that would have been a problem if somebody hadn't decided that The Realm's ships weren't much better than a Trireme. The Realm should have been rocking a crazy navy with Artifact flagships that could at least put up a fight against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T19:58:38-07:00","id":1342261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342237#post1342237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death lords weren't exactly competent in the past. They were all to wrapped up in their passion plays to accomplish anything. The only Deathlord that I recall being more dangerous than an 80's cartoon villain going mwahaha in their secret lair was the Bodhisattva and his First Age Doom Fleet. I doubt that would have been a problem if somebody hadn't decided that The Realm's ships weren't much better than a Trireme. The Realm should have been rocking a crazy navy with Artifact flagships that could at least put up a fight against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Prince is an example of that problem multiple-fold.<br /> <br /> First, the Doomfleet in effect erased anything interesting fo the rest of Skullstone. It was a genuinely <i>interesting</i> culture that was alien and weird. That it's all built on an effective holocaust with the ultimate goal of Murder Everything undermines it, since no one talks about Skullstone as anything more than an existential threat to the setting, rather than a part of it.<br /> <br /> The second a bit is that the Silver Prince's portrayal up to that point had a vibe of &quot;Cultural Victory Deathlord&quot; to it, which gets undermined when in the end it's a ploy for again, Soulsteel Weapon Holocaust.<br /> <br /> It also kind of ties a bit with the way 2e put artifice as while impressive, soemthing that only matters when massed to a certain scale, and that particular kinds of artifice (magitech, whcih all vehicles were) was the teleological course of all advanced societies in Creation.<br /> <br /> And again, this all comes from preseting Deathlords as ultimatelya bout Killing Everything.<br /> <br /> Note, 1e, wasn't a lot better. The entire &quot;Deathlords are actually incompetent ghosts&quot; coms a bit because the First and Forsaken Lion's portrayal was so overwelming in the last end of th eline you had to assume they were incompetent or the world was fucked eight times over by now. Which leads to less interesting and to an extent, less useful, Deathlords.<br /> <br /> Note also that 2e also ahd the Dowager, who was presented as actually competent, just working on a pretty big &quot;All eggs in one basket&quot; plotline that again, didn't leave much fo ryou to <i>do</i> with her that wasn't a doomsday scenario.<br /> <br /> This is a bit why I note taking Oblivion as a major thing out of the picture ultimatley probably helps things. Plus generally trying to not write them as nine varieties of Sauron.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T23:11:05-07:00","id":1342283,"title":"","content":"Actually from 1st ed my impression wasn't that the Lion was incompetent, but rather that he didn't actually want to destroy everything, and it was for betraying them and saving the world in the Contagion the Neverborn had cursed him. That's how I ran him. 2nd ed played this down though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T01:08:34-07:00","id":1342305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342261#post1342261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also kind of ties a bit with the way 2e put artifice as while impressive, soemthing that only matters when massed to a certain scale, and that particular kinds of artifice (magitech, whcih all vehicles were) </div> </div> </div> </div>I realise you're making a point about Isle 5. But I had a 3 year Solar game set on our Folding Ship of Land and Water which was not magi-tech. Plus airboats.<br /> <br /> Certainly magitech dominated the 2E paradigm, and my longest 2E game was set on one of those vehicles that was a mobile artifact factory. But not <i>all</i> vehicles were magitech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T04:22:50-07:00","id":1342327,"title":"","content":"Magitech is a change but not so absolute. Basically as I see it 2e probably had a rash of &quot;tech&quot; / magical stuff looks like tech as a influence and badge of pride that this was permitted in JRPG, pulp and anime fantasy influences (which are pretty gleefully promiscuous in the scope of imagination) but not in your average traditional D&amp;D fantasy spinoff setting of the late 90s (which had many influences but are in many ways dominated by acting as a heir to Tolkien and other such that try to create a &quot;High Fantasy&quot; image of a time of ancient myth without industrial technology).<br /> <br /> It's kind of a &quot;This is not your average standard fantasy RPG setting&quot; talking point and people explore this to the max. It's part of the &quot;Not your average standard AD&amp;D like fantasy&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Then this no longer becomes as cool because it's a bit more normalized across TTRPGs - not that there weren't any before, but you have a lot more things besides Exalted out playing with similar ideas. And over Exalted itself tends to suffer from magitech becoming a vector for over-emphasis by a certain kind of fan fixating on reborn Twilight Caste Solars easily fixing everything single handed with a shake of the Craft rules, and of setting over-emphasis on Autocthon.<br /> <br /> So because of all this it makes sense to dial it down a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T07:26:16-07:00","id":1342342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342305#post1342305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realise you're making a point about Isle 5. But I had a 3 year Solar game set on our Folding Ship of Land and Water which was not magi-tech. Plus airboats.<br /> <br /> Certainly magitech dominated the 2E paradigm, and my longest 2E game was set on one of those vehicles that was a mobile artifact factory. But not <i>all</i> vehicles were magitech.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Folding and Land Ships were the only non-magitech artifact vehicles in 2e to my memory. The first book we got vehicle rules in, presented them in the context of magitech. Note Haslanti airboats were themselves not artifacts at all. But the ones with artifact engines? Those engines were magitech. And note, that those two vehicles were in the third Book of Sorcery almost two years after 2e's launch. <b>Wonders of the Lost Age</b> was the very first main sourcebook for the line, and did a lot to contexualize what was important for artifacts in that edition. (<b>Arms of the Chosen</b>, notably, tries to do the same.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T11:54:08-07:00","id":1342386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342342#post1342342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Folding and Land Ships were the only non-magitech artifact vehicles in 2e to my memory. The first book we got vehicle rules in, presented them in the context of magitech. Note Haslanti airboats were themselves not artifacts at all. But the ones with artifact engines? Those engines were magitech. And note, that those two vehicles were in the third Book of Sorcery almost two years after 2e's launch. <b>Wonders of the Lost Age</b> was the very first main sourcebook for the line, and did a lot to contexualize what was important for artifacts in that edition. (<b>Arms of the Chosen</b>, notably, tries to do the same.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, i always liked Oadenol's Codex far more and always felt that Wonders coming first was something of a misstep from 2e even back then, among other things because the magitech stuff was pretty much inspired/ripped from Outcaste &amp; Autochtonians, that were late books in 1e's run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-19-2019, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T13:52:38-07:00","id":1342400,"title":"","content":"I preferred Oedanal's, as it had more variety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:43:47-07:00","id":1342514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342400#post1342400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I preferred Oedanal's, as it had more variety.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It had an emphasis of the fantastic over &quot;tech gear as magic&quot; take that i enjoyed, so the fact 3e follows the same direction overall really pleases me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, i like some of the tweaks and changes done to elementals in 3e - very much the fact the elementals are more emphasized as beings of the physical world that may have come to be in a number of ways, long before the Divine Revolution, unrecognized since Creation's heyday, somewhere between beast, strange nonhuman races, godblood or other things besides.<br /> <br /> Equally important, the rewrite of summon elemental as an act of actual crafting/creation solves the &quot;i'll summon Fakharu/Wong Bongerok/insert your lesser elemental dragon major NPC &amp; make it my 8itch&quot; issue, while opening room for new venues for PCs and STs to explore with them, be it the formation of whole new, custom, unique elementals, by accident or intent, through the interplay of elemental associations or the roleplaying opportunities in the dynamics between summoner &amp; summon that may potentially run the gamut from master-servant to parent-child to maker-maid or or a number of other options. But the period of service is now also a formative period for the elemental, what may lead into a number of things depending if it survives or not.<br /> <br /> And i'm not even going into the issue of how &quot;born&quot; elementals with cultures and histories of their own might or not feel about those created into their image through Sorcery, what might run a pretty varied gamut of views, reactions or prejudices too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-20-2019, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T15:45:05-07:00","id":1342588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342514#post1342514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It had an emphasis of the fantastic over &quot;tech gear as magic&quot; take that i enjoyed, so the fact 3e follows the same direction overall really pleases me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, i like some of the tweaks and changes done to elementals in 3e - very much the fact the elementals are more emphasized as beings of the physical world that may have come to be in a number of ways, long before the Divine Revolution, unrecognized since Creation's heyday, somewhere between beast, strange nonhuman races, godblood or other things besides.<br /> <br /> Equally important, the rewrite of summon elemental as an act of actual crafting/creation solves the &quot;i'll summon Fakharu/Wong Bongerok/insert your lesser elemental dragon major NPC &amp; make it my 8itch&quot; issue, while opening room for new venues for PCs and STs to explore with them, be it the formation of whole new, custom, unique elementals, by accident or intent, through the interplay of elemental associations or the roleplaying opportunities in the dynamics between summoner &amp; summon that may potentially run the gamut from master-servant to parent-child to maker-maid or or a number of other options. But the period of service is now also a formative period for the elemental, what may lead into a number of things depending if it survives or not.<br /> <br /> And i'm not even going into the issue of how &quot;born&quot; elementals with cultures and histories of their own might or not feel about those created into their image through Sorcery, what might run a pretty varied gamut of views, reactions or prejudices too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also one of my favorite bits actually. That elementals are exotic but still important parts of the world to me do a lot of the &quot;Creation runs on different rules&quot; a lot better than I think at times 2e tried to do wtih it as well. And it also gives a lot more play with elementals as spirits when you don't have this lingering &quot;They're all fundementally lesser broken things than the real originals' is just tossed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:44:21-07:00","id":1342767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342588#post1342588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also one of my favorite bits actually. That elementals are exotic but still important parts of the world to me do a lot of the &quot;Creation runs on different rules&quot; a lot better than I think at times 2e tried to do wtih it as well. And it also gives a lot more play with elementals as spirits when you don't have this lingering &quot;They're all fundementally lesser broken things than the real originals' is just tossed out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fact the origins &amp; nature of both Sorcery and elementals are more open-ended and left up to the individual gaming groups interepretation is a major plus.<br /> That and throwing the whole &quot;gods are prejudiced against elementals - and terrestrial exalted, that just happen to be elementally-aspected too&quot; balderdash in the Mouth of Void, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my own games i have found them useful in covering a number of niches between exotic/non-human people, monsters and gods or exalted. Very nice for when you want something weirder and with more omph than a beastman or wyld mutant but still all too mundane and physical in outlook overall. Or not, i have twisted my own takes on the subject too.<br /> <br /> They do make a pretty good tool to port races of creatures from other settings with little to no changes or one or two funky twists along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-21-2019, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:06:59-07:00","id":1342787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342767#post1342767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> They do make a pretty good tool to port races of creatures from other settings with little to no changes or one or two funky twists along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any example you may have? I have never thought about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T06:23:31-07:00","id":1342930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342787#post1342787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any example you may have? I have never thought about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters i guess, satyrs as a primordial race of wandering woodlands spirits of time-lost origins that personify reproductive urges and the excess or loss of control associated with them in all living things, attracting mortal, beast and more to their wild revels through their magical songs, through which they collects samples of hair, skin, blood, tears and other fluids, used by them to either obtain the secret of new shapes or blend in the crafting of exotic composite new living beings as artworks of sorts, gifts that some savants and exalts associate with the blessing of Gaia and Luna (i started them as just reskined Neomah, but the theming went so well they pretty much gained a life of their own in the game).<br /> <br /> Beside them, loads of stuff from D&amp;D - though a good chunk of that are critters itself derived from folklore &amp; myth, like pretty much all main giants &amp; giant-kin, behir, salamanders, azer and a bunch of other monsters, using some straight with names and all, others renamed and with minimal bits of fluff to fit in Creation, &quot;orks&quot; being called greenmaws, a race of green skinned, fanged elementally-touched barbarians that worship the elementals/carnivorous of the same name as their ancestors/patrons, among other things. Some Magic the Gathering critters too, thought sometimes i mix and match so much i even forget individual examples.<br /> <br /> Also toyed with adapting yordles from League of Legends as some sort of elemental race instead of fae, but left it aside as i'm not that really familiar with LoL lore anyway.<br /> <br /> The greater part of them are just passing references or a quick encounter or bit of exposition. Overall it's more about how one uses a number of themes elementals now more clearly cover as inspiration to cook up either new races or individuals. My personal set of rough guidelines you can see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals/page2\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2019, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T09:50:25-07:00","id":1342961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342930#post1342930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for starters i guess, satyrs as a primordial race of wandering woodlands spirits of time-lost origins that personify reproductive urges and the excess or loss of control associated with them in all living things, attracting mortal, beast and more to their wild revels through their magical songs, through which they collects samples of hair, skin, blood, tears and other fluids, used by them to either obtain the secret of new shapes or blend in the crafting of exotic composite new living beings as artworks of sorts, gifts that some savants and exalts associate with the blessing of Gaia and Luna (i started them as just reskined Neomah, but the theming went so well they pretty much gained a life of their own in the game).<br /> <br /> Beside them, loads of stuff from D&amp;D - though a good chunk of that are critters itself derived from folklore &amp; myth, like pretty much all main giants &amp; giant-kin, behir, salamanders, azer and a bunch of other monsters, using some straight with names and all, others renamed and with minimal bits of fluff to fit in Creation, &quot;orks&quot; being called greenmaws, a race of green skinned, fanged elementally-touched barbarians that worship the elementals/carnivorous of the same name as their ancestors/patrons, among other things. Some Magic the Gathering critters too, thought sometimes i mix and match so much i even forget individual examples.<br /> <br /> Also toyed with adapting yordles from League of Legends as some sort of elemental race instead of fae, but left it aside as i'm not that really familiar with LoL lore anyway.<br /> <br /> The greater part of them are just passing references or a quick encounter or bit of exposition. Overall it's more about how one uses a number of themes elementals now more clearly cover as inspiration to cook up either new races or individuals. My personal set of rough guidelines you can see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals/page2\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must say I love your satyrs :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T08:11:17-07:00","id":1343177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342961#post1342961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I must say I love your satyrs :O</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, i did luck out with them in the &quot;mix elemental associations &amp; mythic creature handy&quot; part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T12:20:22-07:00","id":1343240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1342261#post1342261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also kind of ties a bit with the way 2e put artifice as while impressive, soemthing that only matters when massed to a certain scale, and that particular kinds of artifice (magitech, whcih all vehicles were) was the teleological course of all advanced societies in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I didn't dislike magitech on principle.<br /> <br /> I disliked the level of industrialisation present in the First Age coupled with the significant number of NPCs who remember that era, not enough to help you rebuild it but enough to sneer at how everything is shit now. So they see a Solar who is so proud of the fact that she rebuilt an airship from scrap and upgraded it in the process... but to their frame of reference they\u2019re looking at a ricer car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T12:43:18-07:00","id":1343243,"title":"","content":"Maybe the first age could have had, like, a techy kingdom or something. <br /> <br /> Just a place that had that sort of aesthetic at one point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T12:56:47-07:00","id":1343246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343243#post1343243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the first age could have had, like, a techy kingdom or something.<br /> <br /> Just a place that had that sort of aesthetic at one point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It as an aesthetic is fine. It as a whole special to its own superior sort of artifice is the issue I tend to push back against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T15:36:00-07:00","id":1343290,"title":"","content":"Third Edition is perfectly fine with magitech aesthetics. They don't even need to be associated with the First Age; your Solar crafter can build armor with glowing Tron lines if you like! The aesthetic just doesn't come with mechanical benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T19:16:04-07:00","id":1343319,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the industrial as mechanically superior never really made sense. Factories and the Industrial revolution saw a massive decline in the quality of most goods. Anything a factory can make, a craftsman with tools of the same precision can make better. That is to say, of higher quality and greater reliability.<br /> <br /> The difference is that while a craftsman can make a really good thing in a day or so, a factory can make 100 barely adequate things in an hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T01:30:37-07:00","id":1343358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343243#post1343243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the first age could have had, like, a techy kingdom or something.<br /> <br /> Just a place that had that sort of aesthetic at one point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Denandsor seems like a good candidate.<br /> Also, a detail from 2nd edition that's been retained in the 3e Brass Legionaire write-up is that they started out looking like simulacra soldiers and got progressively more robot-like with each generation.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T03:22:03-07:00","id":1343371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343319#post1343319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the industrial as mechanically superior never really made sense. Factories and the Industrial revolution saw a massive decline in the quality of most goods.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the locomotives they had prior to that wweree just awful.<br /> <br /> I don't think people's fixations on magitech are concerned with the quality of cloth or furniture it's putting out, they care about the machines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T03:48:39-07:00","id":1343373,"title":"","content":"There's also a difference in economics.<br /> <br /> The idea that industrial factory products are inherently inferior is skipping the huge impact of capitalism. Once you can produce items at an industrial scale, anything that's intended for regular people declines in quality because you want to sell them a new product on a regular basis so you have someone to sell all that production capability too.<br /> <br /> If your factories are focused on catering to the super-elite (aka the Exalts) quality goes up significantly. There's no superior artisanal super-car, mega-yacht, or private jet. Those still get made in factories just like the regular old stuff does. Expensive custom fitted suits and dresses still use factory made fabrics and other materials. Etc. Magitech is still dealing in artifice, which means most of it isn't really meant for regular folks; it's meant for the Exalts and their direct servants.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T05:11:06-07:00","id":1343383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343371#post1343371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the locomotives they had prior to that wweree just awful.<br /> <br /> I don't think people's fixations on magitech are concerned with the quality of cloth or furniture it's putting out, they care about the machines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Locomotives were outright impossible without massive increase in quantity of steel produced, just because of how much you needed for the rails. Make no mistake, quantity is a quality all its own, and it led to a massive increase of what a society as a whole was capable of. But that's very different from industrially produced things being of superior quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T05:33:37-07:00","id":1343386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343358#post1343358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denandsor seems like a good candidate.<br /> Also, a detail from 2nd edition that's been retained in the 3e Brass Legionaire write-up is that they started out looking like simulacra soldiers and got progressively more robot-like with each generation.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That pic in Arms of the Chosen showing the evolution of the Brass Legionaires is, I think, my favourite one from the book.<br /> <br /> Although I have reread their entry in Creatures of the Wyld, and that detail is from their first apparition there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T06:08:11-07:00","id":1343393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343383#post1343383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Locomotives were outright impossible without massive increase in quantity of steel produced</div> </div> </div> </div>And you know, needing machines to produce the components.<br /> <br /> You're not getting the parts for them out of a smithy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's very different from industrially produced things being of superior quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>What things? &quot;Things&quot; is the single most all-encompassing to the point of useless category there is.<br /> <br /> Some industrially produced things were of inferior quality... for a little while. A lot of modern clothing has numerous merits over what was once produced by hand with the tools available.<br /> <br /> Some things are impossible to manufacture without industrial machining, and they have a number of benefits. The manner in which we're communicating, for instance. Can't make the telegraph without industrialisation.<br /> <br /> That's only partially germane to First Age Artifice, although it might provide a few guidelines. It doesn't need to look like real industrialisation, but some of the social effects would greatly transform the Age of Sorrows, and that's the standard defining the Artifice.<br /> <br /> Like, for instance, making clothes a lot easier to manufacture in bulk and reducing their cost. It doesn't need to look like a Victorian mill, but it will be First Age Artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T07:34:12-07:00","id":1343411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343358#post1343358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denandsor seems like a good candidate.<br /> Also, a detail from 2nd edition that's been retained in the 3e Brass Legionaire write-up is that they started out looking like simulacra soldiers and got progressively more robot-like with each generation.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And now i'm thinking of putting city and automata together, along with some imprisoned demons/elementals, angyalkae and a mummified princess in a kind of City of Brass style scenario.<br /> <br /> Yes, i know Denandsor is in the middle of the Scavenger Lands and not the desertic South, like the supposed kingdom of origin of the brass legionaries - or arabian nights tale - but i might play with that a bit too. PCs acquire what seems to be a good map of Denandsor, but everything is wrong - not because the map is false, but the ruin that scavenger lords have tried for centuries to plunder is <b>not </b>Denandsor, but a southern metropolis that switched places with the original Denandsor in the causality-eroding chaos of the Balorian Crusade..... yeah, yeah, need some tweaking to give the players clues and hooks to play with but it could work i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2019, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T10:01:44-07:00","id":1343452,"title":"","content":"Industrial manufacturing is one of the few areas that I might actually be considered an expert in, and I think a few things here might be getting conflated.<br /> <br /> Advanced precision machining, forming, welding, casting, materials science, ect. don\u2019t necessarily have anything to do with mass production or assembly lines, and mass production doesn\u2019t necessarily lead to lower quality, but it kind of does.<br /> <br /> The key to quality production is how much care is being put in at each step, and stuff crafted bespoke by master craftsmen have QA built in at every step. An expert with high precision tools and instruments is shaping each part, checking them, and assembling them. Not to mention professional pride and feeling personally connected to the things they hand craft. With very large volume production a stamping machine that stamps parts out might be slowly losing its edge and with nobody watching it very closely parts start to creep out of spec. The other thing with high volume production is that very little savings on each part lead to massive profits, so production facilities will make things absolutely as cheap as they can get away with. That leads to cutting corners everywhere, cheap machines being fed cheap materials. As long as marketing can still sell it to the customer, it\u2019s good. Depending on the item and the customer that may still be a very high standard of quality.<br /> <br /> So, applying that to the First Age we can have magitech, industry, and mass production in a lot of different combinations. So if you want the Five Metal Shrike with it\u2019s hologlyph displays and Essence circuitry you don\u2019t necessarily need a lot in the way of industrial machinery, especially with Exalted skill, you just have to accept that the shrike was a really serious labor. You don\u2019t even need industrial machines for a big clockwork man, that\u2019s definitely plausible to make by hand.<br /> <br /> If you want an army of clockwork soldiers that gets a lot harder. You\u2019re probably not hand crafting 1,200 gears for each of your 10,000 clockwork warriors, you need a factory that\u2019s cranking out parts, and an assembly line to put them all together. You also need massive material processing facilities. All that high quality iron isn\u2019t going to smelt itself in your little crucible. If you apply that to artifacts that\u2019s how you get a \u201cMark XVII Daiklave, type-S\u201d with a serial number on it as the only thing that distinguishes it from others of its kind. That\u2019s also how you might get cheap quality daiklaves, if you\u2019re producing daiklaves in massive quantities, reducing the amount of Jade used by 3% could give you another 500 daiklaves for the same price. Cutting out two production steps? That shaves down time AND cost, at the price of allowing it to channel most of the evocations that the previous design could. Which is all assuming you allow the concept of industrial production of artifacts anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T10:22:22-07:00","id":1343456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343411#post1343411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And now i'm thinking of putting city and automata together, along with some imprisoned demons/elementals, angyalkae and a mummified princess in a kind of City of Brass style scenario.<br /> <br /> Yes, i know Denandsor is in the middle of the Scavenger Lands and not the desertic South, like the supposed kingdom of origin of the brass legionaries - or arabian nights tale - but i might play with that a bit too. PCs acquire what seems to be a good map of Denandsor, but everything is wrong - not because the map is false, but the ruin that scavenger lords have tried for centuries to plunder is <b>not </b>Denandsor, but a southern metropolis that switched places with the original Denandsor in the causality-eroding chaos of the Balorian Crusade..... yeah, yeah, need some tweaking to give the players clues and hooks to play with but it could work i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ireland/Iceland?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T11:02:50-07:00","id":1343467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343386#post1343386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I have reread their entry in Creatures of the Wyld, and that detail is from their first apparition there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I don't have that book and assumed it was one of the instances where 2e had expanded on first edition lore well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T14:23:56-07:00","id":1343495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343452#post1343452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is all assuming you allow the concept of industrial production of artifacts anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> At some point there are going to be Alchemicals and we'll be revisiting Autochthon, so I have to assume that industrial production of artifacts is possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:10:52-07:00","id":1343500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343495#post1343495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At some point there are going to be Alchemicals and we'll be revisiting Autochthon, so I have to assume that industrial production of artifacts is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you?<br /> <br /> Industrial production in general? Yes.<br /> Of artifacts? I'm not convinced. Let the Champions drawn on Autochthonous industry, but hand-craft their own wonders. Like lightsabers, make assembling a beamklaive an almost spiritual rite of passage instead of renting one from Beams R Us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:20:12-07:00","id":1343503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343456#post1343456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ireland/Iceland?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When it comes to Wyld messing things through twisting of correlations, yes, might be quite possible actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343495#post1343495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At some point there are going to be Alchemicals and we'll be revisiting Autochthon, so I have to assume that industrial production of artifacts is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Much of the autochtonians' infrastructure is quite mundane in nature and what artifacts we have seen were pretty much in the hands of Alchemicals, that weren't much more numerous than solars or lunars last time i checked in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2019, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:38:01-07:00","id":1343511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343503#post1343503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When it comes to Wyld messing things through twisting of correlations, yes, might be quite possible actually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not exactly. Much of the autochtonians' infrastructure is quite mundane in nature and what artifacts we have seen were pretty much in the hands of Alchemicals, that weren't much more numerous than solars or lunars last time i checked in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember 1E, but 2E Alchemicals got three dots of Artifacts for every dot they spent on the Background (Dynasts only got 2, and I think Jadeborn only got 2 as well): so triple the artifacts that Solars/Lunars/Sids got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T16:27:26-07:00","id":1343516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343511#post1343511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember 1E, but 2E Alchemicals got three dots of Artifacts for every dot they spent on the Background (Dynasts only got 2, and I think Jadeborn only got 2 as well): so triple the artifacts that Solars/Lunars/Sids got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they <b>are </b>champions of the state. What in the setting's case means pretty much their whole world as divided by the Eight Nations.<br /> It's even a little better than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Alchemicals, pg. 93</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Alchemical gains three dots worth of artifacts for each point of the Artifact Background he buys.<br /> Alchemicals may even raise their Artifact Background all the way to five dots <b><i>without using bonus points</i></b>,<br /> paying only one Background or bonus point each for the fourth and fifth dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectable on an individual basis, yes indeed, there's no denying - but if their numbers stay the same, they might have as many artifacts as Creation's Celestials counted together - in the Age of Sorrows. Much, much less than even the totality of what might be available to the Scarlet Dynasty when one stops to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2019, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T16:56:10-07:00","id":1343517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343452#post1343452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Industrial manufacturing is one of the few areas that I might actually be considered an expert in, and I think a few things here might be getting conflated.<br /> <br /> Advanced precision machining, forming, welding, casting, materials science, ect. don\u2019t necessarily have anything to do with mass production or assembly lines, and mass production doesn\u2019t necessarily lead to lower quality, but it kind of does.<br /> <br /> The key to quality production is how much care is being put in at each step, and stuff crafted bespoke by master craftsmen have QA built in at every step. An expert with high precision tools and instruments is shaping each part, checking them, and assembling them. Not to mention professional pride and feeling personally connected to the things they hand craft. With very large volume production a stamping machine that stamps parts out might be slowly losing its edge and with nobody watching it very closely parts start to creep out of spec. The other thing with high volume production is that very little savings on each part lead to massive profits, so production facilities will make things absolutely as cheap as they can get away with. That leads to cutting corners everywhere, cheap machines being fed cheap materials. As long as marketing can still sell it to the customer, it\u2019s good. Depending on the item and the customer that may still be a very high standard of quality.<br /> <br /> So, applying that to the First Age we can have magitech, industry, and mass production in a lot of different combinations. So if you want the Five Metal Shrike with it\u2019s hologlyph displays and Essence circuitry you don\u2019t necessarily need a lot in the way of industrial machinery, especially with Exalted skill, you just have to accept that the shrike was a really serious labor. You don\u2019t even need industrial machines for a big clockwork man, that\u2019s definitely plausible to make by hand.<br /> <br /> If you want an army of clockwork soldiers that gets a lot harder. You\u2019re probably not hand crafting 1,200 gears for each of your 10,000 clockwork warriors, you need a factory that\u2019s cranking out parts, and an assembly line to put them all together. You also need massive material processing facilities. All that high quality iron isn\u2019t going to smelt itself in your little crucible. If you apply that to artifacts that\u2019s how you get a \u201cMark XVII Daiklave, type-S\u201d with a serial number on it as the only thing that distinguishes it from others of its kind. That\u2019s also how you might get cheap quality daiklaves, if you\u2019re producing daiklaves in massive quantities, reducing the amount of Jade used by 3% could give you another 500 daiklaves for the same price. Cutting out two production steps? That shaves down time AND cost, at the price of allowing it to channel most of the evocations that the previous design could. Which is all assuming you allow the concept of industrial production of artifacts anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saying what I was trying to much better than I was.<br /> <br /> I would also not allow industrial production of artifacts in 3e as an aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T01:25:55-07:00","id":1343543,"title":"","content":"Dragonblood used to get 2 dots of artefact per dot of the background, but in 3rd ed they don't. So I wouldn't be surprised if the Alchemicals also have their Artefact merit nerfed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T01:41:55-07:00","id":1343545,"title":"","content":"Might get free dots to spend on stuff like dragonblooded do, since they're state-sponsored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T04:36:18-07:00","id":1343559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343516#post1343516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respectable on an individual basis, yes indeed, there's no denying - but if their numbers stay the same, they might have as many artifacts as Creation's Celestials counted together - in the Age of Sorrows. Much, much less than even the totality of what might be available to the Scarlet Dynasty when one stops to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Chosen of Autochthon presently number roughly <br /> 1,000&quot;<br /> <br /> 1000 Exalts with triple artifacts are going to have more artifacts than 800 Exalts with single artifacts.<br /> <br /> (The 10,000 Dragons are going to have more artifacts total.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T06:27:25-07:00","id":1343569,"title":"","content":"The Scarlett Empire is like a kraken, with its mantle sitting on the Blessed Isle and innumerable tentacles stretching out and wending their way through the Threshold, wrapping around anything of value and pulling it towards the maw, which includes both artifacts and Jade, which is specifically valued for its ability to make more artifacts. So if you want alchemicals to have more than that, I think you\u2019re going to need to set up industrial mass production, at least a little. You could maybe make it feel more like the equivalent of shipbuilding, where it\u2019s kind of mass production but it\u2019s so big and so difficult that each production is still kind of unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T06:49:01-07:00","id":1343574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343569#post1343569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlett Empire is like a kraken, with its mantle sitting on the Blessed Isle and innumerable tentacles stretching out and wending their way through the Threshold, wrapping around anything of value and pulling it towards the maw, which includes both artifacts and Jade, which is specifically valued for its ability to make more artifacts. So if you want alchemicals to have more than that, I think you\u2019re going to need to set up industrial mass production, at least a little. You could maybe make it feel more like the equivalent of shipbuilding, where it\u2019s kind of mass production but it\u2019s so big and so difficult that each production is still kind of unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Venice's Arsenal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T09:16:06-07:00","id":1343599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343559#post1343559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The Chosen of Autochthon presently number roughly<br /> 1,000&quot;<br /> <br /> 1000 Exalts with triple artifacts are going to have more artifacts than 800 Exalts with single artifacts.<br /> <br /> (The 10,000 Dragons are going to have more artifacts total.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, should have rechecked their numbers too while i was at it. I thought alchemicals were about 400 for some weird reason i can't remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T11:55:05-07:00","id":1343621,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting though, Abyssal and Infernal artifact backgrounds aimed for mechanical parity with Solars rather than serving as a reflection of how well their masters were willing to equip them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T13:12:08-07:00","id":1343639,"title":"","content":"Something I haven't seen anyone mention is the fact that you can't directly buy dots in Essence in this edition. Your essence rating is now a function of the amount of experience you have spent on your character. Gone are the days of hoarding your experience to then spend months in contemplation raise your current rating. This hopefully encourages the player to keep being an active agent in the world. Solars and Lunars follow the same progression, whereas dragon-blooded, with default character creation rules, start at essence 2, reach essence 3 sooner and then take longer to reach essence 4 and 5.<br /> <br /> Also, beyond your initial merit purchases, many of them can't be bought, simply only available at character creation or gained and lost(!) based on the circumstance of your chronicle (Betray a well-connected associate at the gala? Well, they no longer going to aide you next time you plead for help(allies). Pour your blood, sweat, and tears into creating a breath-taking piece of art and exhibit it for the world to see? You might gain recognition as a skilled artisan(influence) which leads to a following of admirers and patrons(followers and possibly backing), and then some cash if you do sell it(resources) ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T13:24:24-07:00","id":1343641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341778-what-s-changed-between-editions?p=1343574#post1343574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like Venice's Arsenal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an Alchemical is more akin to a modern aircraft carrier in scales of infrastructure and investment than a galleon. I think that's a thing folks miss too. Even with modern engineering capabilites, there are still projects which you need entire nation states to bankroll one or two of. I would think Alchemical Exalted and a lot of Autochthonian society runs on those sort of scales. Just you know, also in the sense of how much is eaten by the indsutrial complex to a point where it still doesn't look very luxurious or that htey're applying things to making it notably better.<br /> <br /> Most Autochthonians live in an environment comparable to 19th Century industrialized facotires and have been for millennia.That indsutrialization results in more shinies inherently I think actually is conflating progress with engineering in a way that's not necessarily the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}